  "title": "Clinical Trials - Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center",
  "text": "Clinical Trials - Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center\nSkip To Main Content\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nLloyd Veterinary Medical Center\nISU CVM\nNews\nCVM Directory\nContacts\nGive Now\nSign Ons\nSearch\nClose Search\nSearch\nSubmit Search\nReferring DVM Login\nToggle Menu\nLloyd Veterinary Medical Center\nClients\nEmergency Services\nMap & Directions\nMake an Appointment\nWhat to Expect\nPayment Policies\nDiscount for ISU Employees, Students and Working Dogs\nGiving\nDr. W. Eugene and Linda Lloyd\nLVMC Client Newsletter\nSmall Animal\nPrimary Care\nSpecialty Care\nSupport Services\nEmergency Services\nStaff Directory\nClinical Trials Center\nHixson-Lied Small Animal Hospital Video\nLarge Animal\nFood Animal & Camelid\nVeterinary Field Services\nSupport Services\nStaff Directory\nEquine\nEquine Field Services\nEquine Internal Medicine\nEquine Intensive Care Unit & Neonatal Intensive Care Unit\nEquine Surgery\nEquine Reproduction\nFarrier\nStaff Directory\nServices\nBlood Donor Program\nInfectious Disease Information\nSupport Services\nVeterinarians\nContact Us\nReferrals\nConsultations\nFollow-up on Mutual Patient\nElectronic Medical Records\nServices\nSurgical Suites Virtual Tour\nVet Pulse\nSmall Animal Directory\nLarge Animal Directory\nReferring DVM Portal Webinars\nContinuing Education\nClinical Trials\nEmployment\nCurrent Openings\nVet Tech & Animal Caretakers Openings\nInternships & Residencies\nISU CVM\nNews\nCVM Directory\nContacts\nGive Now\nSearch\nSubmit Search\nClinical Trial Service\nClinical trials are studies that explore whether a procedure, treatment, diagnostic test, or medical device is safe and effective. Trials help answer questions, and the answers can benefit both animal and human health because of the many diseases common to both. By participating in a clinical trial, you and your pet are helping us advance the future health and well-being of animals and humans.\nThe Lloyd Veterinary Medical Center has outstanding veterinary expertise through its board-certified clinicians, faculty, and technical staff in a state-of-the-art facility. We have expertise and experience in conducting clinical trials and analyzing the data.\nActive Trials\nCardiology\nDog Aging Project\nThe HALT HCM Study\nSpironolactone in dogs with Congestive Heart Failure (CHF)\nEquine\nHorse Owners: Help Advance Protection Against Strangles\n—\nStangvac vaccine Flyer\nInternal Medicine\nBile Acid Assessment in Cats with Chronic Enteropathy\nAssessment of Gastrointestinal Function in Dogs\nOncology\nCerumen as a Biomatrix for Canine Lymphoma Screening\nContact\nWe welcome the opportunity to talk to you about ongoing trials, and whether your pet might be eligible.\nDr. Maria Merodio\nResearch Scientist II\n, Clinical Trial Service\nmmaria@iastate.edu\n515-291-9866\nLloyd Veterinary Medical Center\n1809 S. Riverside Drive\nAmes, IA 50011-3619\n515-294-4900\nAVMA Clinical Trials Database\nFacebook - Small Animal Hospital\nFacebook - Large Animal Hospital\nClients\nSmall Animal\nLarge Animal\nEquine\nServices\nVeterinarians\nClinical Trials\nEmployment\nQuick Links\nISU CVM\nNews\nCVM Directory\nContacts\nGive Now\nLloyd Veterinary Medical Center\n1809 S Riverside Drive\nAmes, Iowa 50011-1134\nSmall Animal\n:\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t515-294-4900\nEquine and Farm Animal\n:\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t515-294-1500\nPrivacy Policy\nNon-discrimination Policy\nDigital Access and Accessibility\nConsumer Information\n© Iowa State University of Science and Technology\n\t\t\t\t2026",
